 "article": {
  "title": "Starting Small: The Science of Tiny Habits",
  "topic": "心理科普（行为科学·习惯养成）",
  "level": "CET-4",
  "words": 336,
  "paras": [
   "Every January, millions of people make the same promise: this year, I will finally get fit, read more, or learn a language. By March, most of them have given up. The problem is not a lack of desire. It is that ambitious goals demand a level of effort and energy that few of us can keep up for long. When the target feels huge, the first step often feels even bigger.",
   "Researchers who study habits have found something surprising. Lasting change does not begin with a burst of motivation; it begins with a very small action repeated again and again. A habit, they explain, is simply a behaviour that the brain has learned to perform almost automatically. The more often we do something, the less energy it takes — until it almost runs on its own.",
   "This is why many teachers now suggest a 'two-minute rule'. Want to run? Start by putting on your running shoes and stepping outside. Want to read more? Begin with a single page. Each action should be so small that it is almost impossible to fail. At first it may seem too easy to matter, but the purpose is not the action itself. It is to build a bridge between intention and behaviour, so that the brain learns: this is who I am now.",
   "The lesson is simple, though not effortless. Willpower is a limited resource that runs out when we are tired or busy. Small, steady steps are not. Rather than relying on a sudden wave of determination, it is wiser to design a routine that almost carries you along. Change, it turns out, rarely arrives all at once; it grows quietly, one small step at a time."
  ],
  "zh": "本文从『新年决心大多失败』说起：目标越大，第一步越难迈出。研究习惯的学者发现，持久的改变不靠一时的干劲，而靠把一个很小的动作反复重复，直到大脑几乎自动完成。据此很多人提倡『两分钟守则』——把起步动作缩到不可能失败，目的是在『意愿』和『行为』之间架桥，让大脑慢慢认定『这就是现在的我』。结论是：别依赖会耗尽的意志力，而要设计一个几乎能推着你走的日常习惯，改变往往是一点一点悄悄长出来的。",
  "hard": [
   {
    "en": "It is that ambitious goals demand a level of effort and energy that few of us can keep up for long.",
    "cn": "问题在于，宏大的目标需要一种极少有人能长期坚持的投入和精力。",
    "why": "这是一个强调句 It is ... that ...；that 从句中又嵌套定语从句 few of us can keep up for long 修饰 effort and energy。写作可用 It is (not A but) B that ... 来强调因果。"
   },
   {
    "en": "The more often we do something, the less energy it takes — until it almost runs on its own.",
    "cn": "我们做得越频繁，耗费的精力就越少——直到它几乎自行运转。",
    "why": "The more ... the less ... 是『越……越……』的比较结构；run on its own（自行运转）是地道的比喻表达，可用于描写系统或习惯。"
   },
   {
    "en": "Rather than relying on a sudden wave of determination, it is wiser to design a routine that almost carries you along.",
    "cn": "与其依赖突如其来的决心，不如设计一个几乎能推着你走的日常习惯。",
    "why": "Rather than + 动名词 作状语，表示『与其……不如』；it is wiser to do 用形式主语；that almost carries you along 是定语从句。"
   }
  ],
